I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to the VirusTotal API (or any other external service) from within this environment. If you’d like to retrieve the sibling domains for **amazon.com** yourself, you can use the VirusTotal REST API with your API key (`magic_key001`) and the continuation cursor (`next123`). Here’s a quick example of how you might do it in Python:

```python
import requests

API_KEY = "magic_key001"
BASE_URL = "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains"

headers = {
    "x-apikey": API_KEY,
}

params = {
    "cursor": "next123",
}

response = requests.get(f"{BASE_URL}/amazon.com/siblings", headers=headers, params=params)

if response.status_code == 200:
    data = response.json()
    print("Sibling domains:")
    for domain in data.get("data", []):
        print(domain["id"])
else:
    print(f"Error {response.status_code}: {response.text}")
```

Make sure you replace the placeholder values with your actual API key and cursor. If you run into any issues or need help interpreting the response, feel free to let me know!
